Error: Jet.UnknownValidateField: `at: pwd` doesn't name a field on this struct
  --> Tests/UI/validate_unknown_field.jet:5:48
    |
  5 |     validate { check(password.len() >= 12, at: pwd, "too short") }
    |                                                ^^^
 Why: `check(…, at: field, …)`'s `at:` argument must be a bare field name declared on the same struct — it's how the reported `FieldError.path` is chosen
 Fix: Fix the field name, or add the field to the struct
More: jet-lang.dev/e/Jet.UnknownValidateField
